es are ringing off the hook and so  we realized we had to do it then because  the demand was so great semester  students on their first day plant a seed  and they go through the whole process of  the plant all the way up to harvest and  at the end we get donate the medicine to  a patient who can't grow for herself  we're currently growing for a patient  named Yvonne white she's confined to a  wheelchair she's an MS patient very soon  we'll we will have graduated 10,000  students classes that we try to  emphasize the most or like legal issues  knowing your rights you know politics  and history and advocacy knowing that I  have the opportunity to reach out and  speak to these students is just  wonderful for me I love the idea of  being able to hopefully activate them  get them out there organizing and  helping us to finally legalize cannabis  once and for all and it's just really  important that people know kind of where  this whole movement came from and where  we're going and really trying to get  people involved because that's the only  way we're gonna be able to accomplish  anything well I am a nurse I'm a  registered nurse with a bachelor's  degree who has run hospice home health  and adult day health care in my County  I'm here because I believe in the  medicine itself that it does work and it  does take care of a lot of ailments and  I believe that our can at our country is  in a prescription drug crisis and I  think that we need to be looking at  alternative medicines for pain and  symptom management it's really  interesting how this whole industry is  shaping up and Oaksterdam University is  really instrumental in providing and  sort of an accreditation  to this we'd love it if your viewers  came on down and signed up for classes  we got lots of spots available coming up  for this summer and fall across the  street is the Bulldog coffee shop it's  the second cannabis outlet in Oaksterdam  one of the reasons we named ourselves  the Bulldog coffee shop our firs