ave to  come arrest this the forces of  opposition Oakland so this is just a  wonderful place to be getting involved  it's kind of the epicenter of the  movement I'd almost say I think  everybody kind of understands that our  current drug policy has failed and by  route taxing and regulating cannabis  will make for safer communities and  allow for the state to have a chance to  get out of its budget deficit California  is a decriminalized state and it's  medical marijuana state and we're still  arresting you know 75,000 people a year  that's outrageous it's a waste of  resources people are really asking  questions about why are we wasting  taxpayers money trying to arrest  prosecute and imprison marijuana  offenders when we could be repeating tax  benefits from a legally regulated market  right now this drug violence going on  down in Mexico it's awful and I can tell  you one thing for certain the drug  cartels do not want you to vote YES on  the tax cannabis and  Americans have a right to drink alcohol  but smoke cigarettes and have guns then  they have a right to smoke a joint it's  as simple as that  [Music]  [Music]

